[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged 412 reports as one known issue. They are three problems.

<ThreeCauses ticket={4471} />

## 1. The parser reads dates month first

The shared parser reads every date month first. Tenants that write the day first get their
dates flipped: 3 October becomes 10 March. This is the bulk of the ticket, and the fix queued
for #4471 covers it.

## 2. The booking-v3 form hints MM/DD/YYYY

Three day-first tenants run booking-v3: `alder.physio`, `copper.studio` and `pale.harbour`.
The form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so their people type month first. The
parser fix does not touch this. The hint needs its own change.

## 3. Bookings land one day off

Five reports are not a flipped day and month. They are a move of one day: "client in Lisbon
got Tuesday, client in Toronto got Monday", an invite that arrived before the booking was
made, a June that is off by one. This points to time zones, not date order. The desk's notes
list them as one-day moves, but the table below files them under the parser by tenant.

<Callout>
